{"is_source_file": true, "format": "Python", "description": "This file implements a QWidget-based widget for visualizing connectivity graphs with nodes representing different network elements (e.g., GW, IRE, Client, RADIO, ETH). It includes functionality for node management, graph layout updates, rendering, and interaction handling such as hover annotations. The class 'ConnectivityMapWidget' manages the core logic, while an internal 'node' class defines node attributes. The file also handles reading network sample data to update the graph accordingly.", "external_files": ["networkx", "PySide2.QtCore", "PySide2.QtWidgets", "matplotlib.backends.backend_qt5", "matplotlib.backends.backend_qt5agg", "matplotlib.pyplot", "pylab"], "external_methods": ["nx.DiGraph", "nx.draw_networkx_nodes", "nx.draw_networkx_edges", "nx.draw_networkx_labels", "nx.get_node_attributes", "self.fig.canvas.mpl_connect", "self.fig.canvas.draw", "self.fig.canvas.draw_idle", "self.logger.getLogger", "self.logger.info", "self.logger.error", "self.logger.exception", "self.logger.debug"], "published": ["add_node_to_graph", "remove_node_by_mac", "readSample", "updateWidthHeight", "closeEvent"], "classes": [{"name": "UpdateSig", "description": "A QObject subclass with a PySide2 Signal that emits an integer, used for triggering graph redraws."}, {"name": "ConnectivityMapWidget", "description": "A QWidget subclass that manages the visualization of a network connectivity graph, including nodes and edges representing network devices and their relationships. It supports dynamic updates, layout recalculations, user interactions, and data parsing to reflect real-time network states."}], "methods": [{"name": "set_node_size_color_label(self, n)", "description": "Sets the visual size, color, and label of a node based on its type and attributes.", "scope": "ConnectivityMapWidget", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "update_hierarchies_from_node(self, n)", "description": "Recursively updates the hierarchy levels of n